          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Engineering careers usually move from graduate trainee to engineer, senior engineer, lead and manager, and each step asks for a different mix of technical depth, cost and schedule control and people leadership, with a choice between specialist and manager tracks along the way."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Early years build technical depth and discipline, middle years add cost, schedule and communication, and senior years add people and business responsibility."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Ask what each level means in the company you join."
          }
        ]
      },
